Subject: URGENT - Foreign Particulate Observed in Insulin Glargine Injection, Batch INS-2026-0034
Date: Mon, 17 Jun 2026 09:22:00 +0000
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"

This is to formally notify AIVOA Pharmaceuticals of an adverse finding during a
routine field inspection at a dispensing pharmacy.

Product: Insulin Glargine Injection, 100 units/mL
Batch/Lot Number: INS-2026-0034
Manufacturing Date: 2026-01-05
Expiry Date: 2027-07-04
Quantity Affected: 3 vials inspected, withheld from dispensing

During inspection, small floating particulate matter was visually observed in the
solution of three vials prior to dispensing. The pharmacist on duty immediately
withheld the affected vials from patient use and escalated internally.

Given the injectable route of administration and potential patient safety
implications, this is classified as a priority complaint requiring urgent
investigation. We request a written response outlining your root cause
investigation and containment actions (including whether other lots from the same
manufacturing run are affected) within 5 business days.

Complaint logged: 2026-06-17

Regards,
J. Martinez
Field Inspector, State Drug Control Office
